llama.cpp (as fetched by Ollama v0.35.1, llama.cpp b11232): CONCAT along
dim 0 with a transposed second operand goes through shared-memory tiles.

WHY
---
Gated DeltaNet layers (Qwen3.5/3.6 and Qwen3-Next, including the MoE
models) build their convolution input as concat(conv_state,
transpose(qkv), dim 0): qkv is a contiguous [channels, tokens] tensor, and
its transpose has the token index strided by the channel count. The CUDA
backend handled that with its generic non-contiguous kernel, which walks
dst rows: every lane's read of src1 lands nb10 bytes from its neighbour's,
32 KiB for 8192 channels. On an RX 590 one such concat (3 + 2048 columns,
8192 rows, f32) took 27 ms, 4.9 GB/s, and the 30 of them in a 2048-token
batch of Qwen3.6 35B-A3B took 0.83 s of the GPU's 5.4 s.

The new kernel reads src1 in 32x32 tiles along its contiguous index and
writes them along dst's rows. blockIdx.x walks the contiguous index as
well: with tiles ordered along the token index instead, workgroups running
together read rows a power of two apart, which on gfx803 all map to one
DRAM channel (9.3 ms for the same concat).

Measured on an RX 590:
  test-backend-ops perf CONCAT f32 [3,8192] + transposed [2048,8192]:
    27 ms -> 1.14 ms (110 GB/s).
  llama-bench Qwen3.6 35B-A3B Q4_K_M, all experts in system RAM
  (-ncmoe 99), pp2048: ubatch 1024 224 -> 233 tok/s, ubatch 2048
  244 -> 270 tok/s.
  test-backend-ops CONCAT 193/193 against the CPU backend, with added cases
  for a transposed src1 (f32 and f16, odd sizes, ne2/ne3 > 1, a viewed
  src0); those cases are not part of this patch.

The slow path is not specific to gfx803; only gfx803 was measured.

WHAT
----
In ggml/src/ggml-cuda/concat.cu, concat_dim0_src1_transposed handles dim 0
when src1's ne[1] is its contiguous index and dst is contiguous along dim
0; the first ne00 columns of each dst row come from src0 in the same
launch. Every other case keeps the existing kernels.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/concat.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/concat.cu
index 6df89013c..e085d0275 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/concat.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/concat.cu
@@ -139,6 +139,63 @@ static __global__ void __launch_bounds__(CUDA_CONCAT_BLOCK_SIZE)
     }
 }
 
+// dim 0 with src1 a transposed view (its ne[1] is the contiguous index), as
+// in the DeltaNet conv input: [conv state | transpose(qkv)]. The generic
+// kernel below walks dst rows, so each lane of src1's reads lands nb10 bytes
+// from the next (32 KiB for 8192 channels): 16.8M elements took 27 ms on an
+// RX 590. src1 goes through 32x32 tiles in shared memory instead, read along
+// its contiguous index and written along dst's rows. blockIdx.x walks that
+// contiguous index too, so workgroups running together read neighbouring
+// pieces of the same src1 rows rather than rows a power of two apart.
+#define CONCAT_T_TILE 32
+#define CONCAT_T_ROWS 8
+template <typename T>
+static __global__ void concat_dim0_src1_transposed(
+        const char * __restrict__ src0, const char * __restrict__ src1, char * __restrict__ dst,
+        const int64_t ne00, const int64_t ne10, const int64_t ne1, const int64_t ne2,
+        const uint64_t nb01, const uint64_t nb00, const uint64_t nb02, const uint64_t nb03,
+        const uint64_t nb10, const uint64_t nb12, const uint64_t nb13,
+        const uint64_t nb1, const uint64_t nb2, const uint64_t nb3) {
+    __shared__ T tile[CONCAT_T_TILE][CONCAT_T_TILE + 1];
+
+    const int64_t i2 = blockIdx.z % ne2;
+    const int64_t i3 = blockIdx.z / ne2;
+    const int64_t i0_base = (int64_t) blockIdx.y * CONCAT_T_TILE;
+    const int64_t i1_base = (int64_t) blockIdx.x * CONCAT_T_TILE;
+
+    const char * s1 = src1 + i3*nb13 + i2*nb12;
+    char       * d  = dst  + i3*nb3  + i2*nb2;
+
+    for (int j = threadIdx.y; j < CONCAT_T_TILE; j += CONCAT_T_ROWS) {
+        const int64_t i0 = i0_base + j;
+        const int64_t i1 = i1_base + threadIdx.x;
+        if (i0 < ne10 && i1 < ne1) {
+            tile[j][threadIdx.x] = *(const T *)(s1 + i0*nb10 + i1*sizeof(T));
+        }
+    }
+    __syncthreads();
+    for (int j = threadIdx.y; j < CONCAT_T_TILE; j += CONCAT_T_ROWS) {
+        const int64_t i1 = i1_base + j;
+        const int64_t i0 = i0_base + threadIdx.x;
+        if (i0 < ne10 && i1 < ne1) {
+            *(T *)(d + i1*nb1 + (ne00 + i0)*sizeof(T)) = tile[threadIdx.x][j];
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (blockIdx.y == 0) {
+        const char * s0 = src0 + i3*nb03 + i2*nb02;
+        for (int j = threadIdx.y; j < CONCAT_T_TILE; j += CONCAT_T_ROWS) {
+            const int64_t i1 = i1_base + j;
+            if (i1 >= ne1) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            for (int64_t i0 = threadIdx.x; i0 < ne00; i0 += CONCAT_T_TILE) {
+                *(T *)(d + i1*nb1 + i0*sizeof(T)) = *(const T *)(s0 + i1*nb01 + i0*nb00);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
